title: Handle relay v3→v2 scheduling rollback for v3-capable parachains

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      A v3-capable parachain falls back to v2 candidates when the relay chain disables the
      `CandidateReceiptV3` node feature, instead of stalling. "V3 active" is now derived from the
      para's `V3_SCHEDULING_ENABLED` const and the relay feature, read from the committed state
      proof via a new decode-only `RelayHostConfigurationPrefix`. The `CoreInfo` digest's
      `claim_queue_offset` bound adds `relay_parent_offset` only on the v2 fallback.

      The slot-based collator reads the scheduling values at the parent it builds on rather than at
      the best head, so they come from the runtime that executes the block.
crates:
  - name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
    bump: patch
  - name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
    bump: patch
  - name: polkadot-primitives
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-primitives-core
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-test-relay-sproof-builder
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
    bump: none
